" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1943: After Italy's armistice the NDH declares the Treaties of Rome void and annexes the Dalmatian lands ceded to Italy</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="560.0" x2="560.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="560.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="560.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>August 1944: The Lorković-Vokić coup against Pavelić fails and its conspirators are executed</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">8</text><title>May 1945: NDH forces and civilians retreat to Austria; the British hand them to the Partisans, and the state falls after the Battle of Odžak on 25 May</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1941 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1945 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1941</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavko-kvaternik">Slavko Kvaternik</a> proclaims the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a> under German protection</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1941</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-pavelic">Ante Pavelić</a> returns from exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and takes power as Poglavnik</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1941</span><span class="rf-text">The Treaties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> cede central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, most Adriatic islands and other lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1941</span><span class="